      "page_title": "Anti-Patterns, Secrets & Digest Pinning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Picking One"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why does `docker exec -it app sh` fail on my distroless image?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "There is no shell in the image at all",
            "Use the `:debug` variant or `docker debug`",
            "Static compiled binary → scratch or distroless-static",
            "JVM, Node, Python needing glibc → distroless-* or slim",
            "Need an ops shell in production → alpine or slim"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "docker run --rm -it \\",
            "  --entrypoint=sh app:debug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Compare On Four Axes",
          "text": "Size, build time, CVE surface, debuggability. And this is all about the final stage — the builder should stay fat and full of tools."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Big Five",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Anti-pattern",
            "Why it hurts",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "COPY . . first",
              "reinstalls deps",
              "split manifest"
            ],
            [
              "split apt update",
              "stale index",
              "chain &&"
            ],
            [
              "rm in later RUN",
              "no size win",
              "same RUN or stage"
            ],
            [
              "ARG secret",
              "in docker history",
              "--mount=secret"
            ],
            [
              "FROM latest",
              "not reproducible",
              "pin digest"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Secrets Done Right"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ARG NPM_TOKEN  # ✗ readable in history",
            "RUN --mount=type=secret,id=npmrc,\\",
            "    target=/root/.npmrc npm ci",
            "# ✓ never lands in any layer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Downloads With Proof"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ADD --checksum=sha256:$SHA \\",
            "  https://x/f.tgz /   # ✓ verified",
            "# syntax < 1.6 → curl + verify:",
            "RUN curl -fsSL -o f.tgz https://x/f.tgz \\",
            " && echo \"$SHA f.tgz\" | sha256sum -c"
          ],
          "note": "--checksum: remote URLs only"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pin And Refresh"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`node:latest` means surprise major-version breakage",
            "Pin `node:20.11.1-alpine` or a full digest",
            "CI reusing a `latest` cache without `--pull` misses patches",
            "The base tag moved upstream; you kept the old bits"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20        # ✗ floats weekly",
            "FROM node:20.11.1-alpine  # better",
            "FROM node@sha256:9f0c...  # ✓ frozen"
          ],
          "note": "digest pin survives a moved tag"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Non-Root Users & Choosing a Base Image",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Never Ship As Root"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN adduser --system app",
            "USER app        # or USER 65532:65532",
            "# default USER is root: escape = root"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`USER` applies to every later RUN, CMD and `exec`",
            "scratch and distroless have no `adduser` — go ==numeric==",
            "Own the app dir at copy time: `COPY --chown=app:app`",
            "Root inside the container is **root** after a kernel escape"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Base Image Cheat Sheet",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Base",
            "libc",
            "Shell",
            "Size"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "alpine",
              "musl",
              "busybox sh",
              "~7MB"
            ],
            [
              "debian-slim",
              "glibc",
              "bash",
              "~75MB"
            ],
            [
              "distroless",
              "glibc",
              "none",
              "~2-50MB"
            ],
            [
              "scratch",
              "none",
              "none",
              "0MB"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Alpine Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Alpine ships ==musl==, so glibc-only manylinux wheels never match and pip compiles C extensions from source. Builds run **5-10x** slower and the image can end up larger than slim once gcc is in.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "DNS edge cases: `search` domains, TCP fallback",
            "Smaller default thread stack → overflow in some runtimes",
            "Older musl malloc lagged under heavy threading",
            "Unsure? `python:3.12-slim` is the boring right default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scratch Needs Certs"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM scratch",
            "COPY --from=build \\",
            "  /etc/ssl/certs/ /etc/ssl/certs/",
            "USER 65532:65532  # numeric only"
          ],
          "note": "no /etc/passwd, /tmp or tzdata"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "No Such File Or Directory",
          "text": "A dynamically linked binary in scratch fails on the missing **loader**, not on your binary. Build static with `CGO_ENABLED=0` or match the runtime base."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Verify Before You Push"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run --rm img id  # uid≠0",
            "docker image inspect img \\",
            "  --format '{{.Config.User}}'"
          ],
          "note": "empty User field means root"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "History Is Readable",
          "text": "`docker history <img>` prints every build arg and command. Anything you passed as ARG belongs to whoever pulls the image."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reproducibility & Node, Python, Go Recipes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Reproducibility Kit",
          "items": [
            "Pin the base by __digest__, never by tag",
            "Commit the lockfile — `npm ci` refuses without one",
            "`BUILDKIT_INLINE_CACHE=1` ships cache metadata",
            "Weekly `--no-cache --pull` so CVE fixes land"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Surface And Churn"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "curl, vim, netcat, build-essential in prod: size and attack surface",
            "No `.dockerignore`: huge context, cache churn, leaked secrets",
            "`.git` drags hundreds of MB and changes every commit",
            "One giant RUN: great size, rebuilds the toolchain on any change"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Node: Build Stage",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20-alpine AS build",
            "WORKDIR /app",
            "COPY package*.json ./",
            "RUN npm ci",
            "COPY . .",
            "RUN npm run build"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Node: Runtime Stage"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20-alpine",
            "WORKDIR /app",
            "COPY package*.json ./",
            "RUN npm ci --omit=dev",
            "COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Ship It Safely"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "USER node",
            "CMD [\"node\",\"dist/main.js\"]  # exec form",
            "HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s \\",
            "  CMD [\"node\",\"health.js\"]",
            "LABEL org.opencontainers.image.source=$REPO"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Python: slim + venv"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM python:3.12-slim AS build",
            "RUN python -m venv /opt/venv",
            "COPY requirements.txt .",
            "RUN /opt/venv/bin/pip install \\",
            "  --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Go Recipe"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`go mod download` before `COPY . .`",
            "`CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags=\"-s -w\"`",
            "Final base: `gcr.io/distroless/static:nonroot`",
            "Shell-form CMD wraps in `/bin/sh -c` and swallows SIGTERM"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 3 of DOCKER IMAGES: LAYERS, CACHE, LEAN BUILDS. Your 1.1GB Node image and your cache miss on every single push are the same bug: you put the thing that changes most at the bottom of the stack. This handbook walks the actual mechanics — union filesystem layers, whiteout files that keep deleted bytes shipping forever, what really goes into a cache key, and why `rm -rf` in a later RUN saves you exactly zero megabytes. Ten pages, ending at 150MB with a non-root user and pinned digests.",
